OGiE5WM5GQdiX","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-08T08:42:43Z","updated_at":"2022-07-08T09:51:01Z","body":"Hi @metrue !\r\n\r\n> Are you talking about the graphql schema validation?\r\n\r\nNo, I want to validate Request *body* or *query parameters*.  For example, \"express-validator\" is similar to what I want to do.\r\n<https://express-validator.github.io/docs/>\r\n\r\nLike \"express-validator\", user can use [validator.js](https://github.com/validatorjs/validator.js). I think it's OK to use this library if user wants to validate it perfectly. But, I want to have more tiny validator for casual use. It will be built-in middleware.\r\n\r\nAlthough, I don't have a plan for validation syntax, API design, and, interface. We'll consider how we make it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1178720407/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1178778337","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/345#issuecomment-1178778337","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/345","id":1178778337,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM5GQrrh","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-08T09:41:33Z","updated_at":"2022-07-08T09:41:33Z","body":"Hi @Code-Hex !\r\n\r\n> I think this is an good example to manage way some middlewares to npm registry.\r\n\r\nThanks for sharing!\r\n\r\n@Code-Hex  @metrue, I've written my thought about the middleware structure: #350 \r\nCheck it out.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1178778337/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1179446684","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/345#issuecomment-1179446684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/345","id":1179446684,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM5GTO2c","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-09T00:48:35Z","updated_at":"2022-07-09T04:22:42Z","body":"I have another idea about a *validator* middleware.\r\n\r\nMake the *validator* middleware as third-party middleware (**not built-in**) using [validator.js](https://github.com/validatorjs/validator.js). The repository will be `github.com/honojs/validator` or in monorepo, package name will be `@honojs/validator`.\r\n\r\nIt depends on the external library but, is easy to implement and it has many rules to validate. \"validator.js\" seems not to depend on other modules, so I think it works on Cloudflare Workers or Deno. We do not need polyfill.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1179446684/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1183178972","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/345#issuecomment-1183178972","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/345","id":1183178972,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM5GheDc","user":{"login":"yusukebe","id":10682,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNjgy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10682?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe","html_url":"https://github.com/yusukebe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yusukebe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-13T12:45:46Z","updated_at":"2022-07-16T08:42:06Z","body":"We have decided to make third-party middleware after v2.0.0 is released. So, the points of this release are:\r\n\r\n- [x]  Support Deno - write test and setup CI\r\n- [x]  Support Bun - make \"serve-static\" middleware for Bun, write test, and setup CI (Currently, some middleware does not work)\r\n- [x] Make new middleware structure for supporting third-party middleware\r\n- [x] Make \"body-parse\" middleware obsolete, make `parseBody()` in Request instead\r\n- [x] Make \"cookie\" middleware obsolete, make `cookie()` in Request and Context instead\r\n- [x] Remove \"graphql-server\" middleware, it might be third-party middleware\r\n- [x] Remove \"mustache\" middleware, it might be third-party middleware\r\n\r\nAlmost done!!\r\n\r\nThe remaining things are:\r\n\r\n- [x] Write document\r\n- [x] Write migration guide\r\n- [x] Make website!!!\r\n\r\nThat time will come soon.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1183178972/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":1,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1184422170","html_url":"https://github.com/honojs/hono/issues/345#issuecomment-1184422170","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/345","id":1184422170,"node_id":"IC_kwDOGiE5WM5GmNka","user":{"login":"metrue","id":1001246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDEyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1001246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue","html_url":"https://github.com/metrue","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/metrue/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2022-07-14T13:03:05Z","updated_at":"2022-07-14T13:03:05Z","body":"Why this item  marked as completed? I did not find any repo github.com/honojs/graphql-server\r\n- [x] Remove \"graphql-server\" middleware, it might be third-party middleware\"","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/honojs/hono/issues/comments/1184422170/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocke